    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0529" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.6176 F 51/41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-06-27T14:00:00-00:44"><hi rendition="#italic">June 27, 1925—2
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>25. The Liberian authorities have delivered to this Legation signed copies of the
                    agreements to be transmitted through the Department of State to Mr. Firestone.
                    Some changes have been made in wording and also a few modifications in an
                    attempt to meet Firestone’s ideas, but they do not affect the spirit or meaning
                    of the agreement.</p>
                <p>The Secretary of State of Liberia is proceeding to America with full power to
                    meet and settle all complications and misunderstandings which may appear.<anchor
                        n="50" xml:id="d374-f1"/> It is necessary that Bussell return
                    immediately.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d374-f1" n="50" xml:id="d374-f1-content">
                <p>The Liberian Secretary of State left Monrovia July 2, arrived in New York August
                    12, and sailed from New York September 26.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
